<title>UK: ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in January.</title>
<headline>ICCO lists buffer stock cocoa for sale in January.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The buffer stock manager of the International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) announced on Monday the buffer stock sales planned for January would total 4,248 tonnes and would comprise the following cocoa, the ICCO said.</p>
<p>The date of the sale has yet to be announced.</p>
<p>Details of the cocoa offered for sale are as follows.</p>
<p>ORIGIN	  TONNES	PORT	CROP	  QUALITY</p>
<p>Cameroon	   25     Amsterdam   1981/82	FF</p>
<p>Cameroon	  100     Amsterdam   1982/83	GF</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire    20     Amsterdam   1979/80	GF</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   351     Amsterdam   1982/83	GF</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   248     Amsterdam   1982/83	FF</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   200     Amsterdam   1983/84	GF</p>
<p>Ghana	   1,244     Hull	  1987/88	GF</p>
<p>Nigeria	    49     Amsterdam   1986/87	GF</p>
<p>Nigeria	    99     Amsterdam   1986/87	FF</p>
<p>Nigeria	   457     Hull	  1986/87	GF</p>
<p>Nigeria	   296     Hull	  1986/87	FF</p>
<p>Nigeria	   100     Hull	  1987/88	GF</p>
<p>The following parcels to be sold as per sample drawn and approved by buyers.</p>
<p>WAREHOUSE KEEPER</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   100   Amsterdam  1979/80   FAQ  Ocean</p>
<p>							Warehousing</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   100   Amsterdam  1981/82   FAQ  Ocean</p>
<p>						  Warehousing</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire   247   Amsterdam  1987/88   FAQ  Handelsveem</p>
<p>Ghana		99   Amsterdam  1987/88   FAQ  Handelsveem</p>
<p>Nigeria	   316   Amsterdam  1980/81   FAQ  Ocean</p>
<p>							Warehousing</p>
<p>Nigeria	   197   Amsterdam  1986/87   FAQ  Handeslveem</p>
<p>GF -- good fermented, FF -- fair fermented, FAQ -- fair to average quality</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
